# PDF Batch Import (Admin)

Turn uploaded DSE question/solution PDFs into per-question cropped `IMG` assets. Admin Operations tool (after Question Ingestion). Backed by [app/pdf_import.py](mdc:app/pdf_import.py); reuses [app/batch_image_gen.py](mdc:app/batch_image_gen.py) for the atomic disk+DB write.

## Flow

```
stage (upload + rasterise) -> detect (SSE, vision LLM per page) -> [review] -> commit (SSE, crop + create rows)
```

- **Automatic mode**: detect SSE writes `plan.json`; on `done` the browser opens commit directly (reads `plan.json`).
- **Review mode** (**live**): the page cards render up-front (each with a "detecting…" status badge) and are **filled in as each page's detection finishes** (`fillPageCard` on every `page` SSE event), so review can start before the whole PDF finishes. A lightweight per-page editor (overlay boxes + crop-preview canvas) lets the admin **drag a box to move, drag handles to resize, Add box (draw on the page), edit qno/label, delete, click a crop thumbnail to enlarge it full-size (`showCropPreview`), or re-run a page with a different method/endpoint**. Boxes are edited in place on the in-memory `plan[kind]` items (`{page,qno|label,box,_uid}`); the live drag/draw system is in [templates/admin_pdf_import.html](mdc:templates/admin_pdf_import.html) (`startDrag`/`onDragMove`/`startDraw`/`finishDraw`/`applyBoxStyle`, pointer-events toggled via `.pdf-page-wrap.adding`). **Add/Delete auto-renumber** the following boxes (exam only; relative shift; see below); manual qno edits and move/resize do not. On Import the edited plan is POSTed to `/plan` (overwrites `plan.json`), then commit runs. Each side also has a **Download deskewed/processed PDF** button. A **Uniform width per side** setup checkbox locks every box on each side (QUE/SOL independently) to one shared width (= the widest box) — resizing one box's width re-broadcasts it to the rest (centres kept); moving stays per-box; untick to free widths. Client-side only (`uniformWidth`/`enableUniformWidth`/`applyUniformWidthToAll`/`snapBoxToUniform` in [templates/admin_pdf_import.html](mdc:templates/admin_pdf_import.html)); the saved plan just keeps the resulting boxes.

One **page image per LLM call** (keeps a small local model — e.g. `qwen3vl4b` — within its context window). Spanning questions = same `qno` on consecutive pages → grouped into a **multi-part** IMG asset (`replace_img_assets(..., stitch=False)`).

## Tasks (exam vs generic)

A top-of-form **Task** toggle (`task=exam|generic`, persisted as `meta['mode']`):

- **Exam paper** (default): question/solution detection → import as `QUE`/`SOL` IMG assets. Question and solution images can target **different versions** — Setup has two selects (`que_version` / `sol_version`, defaults ENO/EN); `iter_commit(..., versions={'que':…,'sol':…}, …)`. **Custom detection prompt** (`meta['custom_prompt']` + `instruction`, Setup checkbox): borrow the context-free generic prompt (textbook / non-standard format) while still importing as `QUE`/`SOL` — `detect_page(..., generic_prompt=True)` returns exam-shaped boxes with `qno=None`, and `iter_detect` **auto-increments** qno per side (running counter); the review UI re-sequences with `renumberAllSequential` (also after a per-page re-run).
- **Generic extraction**: NO exam context. A free-text **instruction** (`meta['instruction']`) drives `build_pdf_generic_system`/`build_pdf_generic_user_text` (+ `parse_generic_boxes` → `{label, box}`). No paper/subject/DB. Review uses a label textbox per region (no qno cascade); the action button is **Download all as ZIP** (`POST /export-zip` → `pdf_import.export_zip_bytes`, crops with `trim_white=False`). Only `que`/single-PDF + `llm`/`refine` (no `segment`).

